# Framework-as-package — the direction the 2026-07-02 biweekly converged on.
schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Framework-as-package
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The toolkit framework as a portable package you drop into a repository, so
    agents can process unstructured resources and data into a knowledge base
    that fits the toolkit's ontology, architecture, and functioning.
  source_traditions: [software packaging, knowledge management, agentic workflows]
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Adopted direction (2026-07-02 planning call, proposed by Luiz). Recommended
    workflow — open a repo, consolidate existing data/resources, bring the
    framework in, agents process the data per the framework, out comes a
    structured knowledge base (ontology, tagging, structure). Initial testable
    version targeted ~2 weeks out; first real cases are Koi's Gen Brasil
    Commons artifacts and Durgadas's Proof of Coordination protocol.
  important_distinctions:
    - ingestion-is-not-storage (Durgadas's design constraint — keep them separable)
    - framework-vs-instance (the package is the framework; each repo it lands in is an instance)
  tensions:
    - portability-vs-opinionated-infrastructure (drop-in-anywhere vs. the push for opinionated infra choices)
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Reducing the framework to a file-format converter — losing the ontology,
    provenance, review states, and return paths that make the knowledge base a
    commons rather than a pile.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: "packages/operations/meetings/260702 Regen Web3 Toolkit Planning Call.md"
    surfaced_by: Luiz Fernando (2026-07-02 planning call)
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
